<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιλάζομαι</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιλά̆β-ῠμαι</span></b> , poet. and 
			Dor.
		 Prose for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιλαμβάνομαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>take hold of, hold by,</i> c.
			gen., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1227
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραγμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theag.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				3.1.67
			</span></i>, cf. Archyt.ib.<i><span class="en">
				117
			</span></i>; <i>take a share of, partake in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					452
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>to receive in turn, to be repaid,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιλάζνται . . τοιάδ᾽ ἃν τοκεῦσι δῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					363
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λάζυμαι</span> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Or.</u>
				753
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IA</u>
				1109
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λάζομαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1227
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Or.</u>
				452
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λάζον</span>); both forms in codd.
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>Med.</u>
				1216
			</span></i>)</div>
